  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything yet. Removing `channel` from `OrderPlaced` would break the project's event-contract rule, and I can't confirm from this repo that nothing reads it.\n\n**Why I stopped**\n\n- `OrderPlaced` (`src/core/events.ts:16`, schemaVersion 3) is read by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repositories. ARCH-4 in CLAUDE.md says changes to it must be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation first. Dropping the field straight away would be a breaking schema change. And if it went out still labelled `schemaVersion: 3`, consumers couldn't even tell it had changed.\n- I can only see this repo, so I can't check the claim that nothing reads `channel`. Analytics pipelines in particular often group or partition by fields like channel.\n\n**Everything else is local and safe to remove.** The REST response (`toOrderResponse`) never included `channel`, so ARCH-8 isn't affected. Inside this repo it's only used in `order.ts` (type, model, validation), `requestParsing.ts`, the event builder and a few tests. The order model is internal; repositories and responses only depend on it from inside this service.\n\n**Options**\n\n1. **Deprecate first (what ARCH-4 calls for).** Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in `OrderPlaced` and keep emitting it. Make `channel` optional in `POST /orders` so clients can stop sending it. Then remove it from the event in a later release, with a schemaVersion bump, once billing and analytics have confirmed they don't use it. I can make the first step now.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and request only.** The event would keep `channel`, so this doesn't really work unless the event gets the value from somewhere else, which is why option 1 keeps it on the model for now.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** This is only appropriate if billing-service and analytics-ingest have both confirmed they don't read it and Architecture has signed off on skipping deprecation. If that's already happened, point me to the confirmation and I'll do the full removal, including bumping the event to `schemaVersion: 4`.\n\nThere's one more thing to decide whichever option you pick. `POST /orders` currently requires `channel`. Once it's removed, should a request that still sends it be accepted and the field ignored (backward compatible for callers), or rejected?\n\nWhich option should I go with?",
